{
 "manufacturer": "Janitza",
 "manufacturer_slug": "janitza",
 "model": "UMG 512-PRO power quality analyser (Modbus RTU / Modbus TCP)",
 "model_slug": "umg-512-pro",
 "short_model": "UMG 512-PRO",
 "aliases": [
  "UMG512-PRO",
  "UMG 512",
  "UMG512",
  "UMG 512 PRO",
  "Janitza UMG512-PRO"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Power meter (power quality analyser)",
 "applies_to": "UMG 512-PRO power quality analyser, per address list 1.054.016.3.k (08/2023).",
 "summary": "The UMG 512-PRO is Janitza's power quality analyser with four voltage and four current channels; the list covers both its RS-485 settings and IP network settings. Measurements are big-endian 32-bit floats that include the CT/VT ratios. This map covers the 19000-19120 'frequently required readings' block, total power factor, the fourth channel sum, energy totals, digital I/O, transformer ratios and the energy reset commands.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU",
  "TCP"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 2,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "Addresses are printed as the protocol address and sent unchanged: 19000 is requested as 19000. The list starts at address 0 (real-time clock), which only fits 0-based numbering. In a 1-based or Modicon tool enter 19001 / 419001."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "Power Quality Analyser UMG 512-PRO - Modbus-address and Formulary",
  "doc_number": "1.054.016.3.k",
  "revision_date": "2023-08",
  "url": "https://www.janitza.com/files/download/manuals/current/UMG512-PRO/janitza-mal-umg512pro-en.pdf",
  "pages": "Functions p. 4; transfer parameters, byte order, number formats p. 5; frequently required readings p. 12; date/time and measured values pp. 13-17; energy pp. 42-49; other values pp. 50-51"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Byte order: the list says its addresses return data big-endian (high byte first, high word in the lower register = ABCD). Adding 32768 to an address returns the same value little-endian; that mirror block is not listed.",
  "Data types in the list: short = signed 16-bit, int = signed 32-bit, uint = unsigned 32-bit, float = IEEE 754 32-bit. Float and integer values include the CT/VT ratios; short values do not.",
  "19068 in the frequently-read block is the consumed energy of tariff 1 (rate 1) only, so it is left out; the all-tariff consumed and delivered totals are taken from the energy table (6508 / 6520).",
  "The energy-table rows 6464-6594 are marked RD/WR in the list (counters can be preset), so they are listed as RW; the same totals in the 19000 block are read-only.",
  "19636 (total power factor) is printed RD/WR; it is a measured value, so do not write it.",
  "Transfer parameters (p. 5): 9.6 to 921.6 kbps, 8 data bits, no parity, the device sends 2 stop bits. The list gives no default baud rate or device address, and no Modbus TCP port.",
  "Left out: device serial number, RS-485 address, mode and baud rows (6856-6864), because the list marks them 'only for internal use'; the strings and internal configuration rows; harmonics, flicker, min/max/mean blocks, event and transient settings.",
  "The list itself does not name Modbus TCP or a TCP port; TCP is listed as a transport because the list carries IP address, mask and gateway settings. Confirm in the device user manual."
 ],
